    <time>1787343443</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>New package: python-graphifyy 0.9.48 (PyPI name graphifyy; CLI is graphify).
Please keep pluskalm as package maintainer.

Devel openSUSE_Tumbleweed is still unresolvable until the TW snapshot
publishes the tree-sitter python grammar bindings already accepted into
Factory. The package builds green where those binaries are visible:
devel ppc64le succeeded, and home:pluskalm:treesitter-py succeeded on
Factory x86_64 and aarch64 (3781 tests passed per flavour).

- Update to 0.9.48:
  * Extractor and graph correctness: directed path queries,
    shrink-guard on incremental merge, language-specific
    call/import resolution, deterministic ids
  * MCP extra is dual-compat with mcp 1.x/2.x and requires
    starlette &gt;= 1.3.1 (CVE-2026-48818, CVE-2026-54283)
  * Optional OCaml and Common Lisp extras (unpackaged)
- Replace spec-cleaner-exploded perl(Git::*) BuildRequires
  with git-core
- Skip test_label_communities_batches_when_over_batch_size:
  batches run concurrently so completion order is racy
- Ship only the GitHub tag archive: the PyPI sdist omits
  tests/fixtures and ARCHITECTURE.md, so the second source
  overlay is unnecessary
- BuildRequires/Recommends the C tree-sitter-&lt;lang&gt; grammar
  libraries: python bindings ctypes-load those shared objects,
  and only tree-sitter-python's python subpackage Requires
  the matching C library
- BuildRequires python-PyYAML so nested Markdown frontmatter
  tests use the YAML parser
- Skip test_built_wheel_ships_the_full_skill_payload: it runs
  python -m build, which collides with OBS's build package
- Pass pytest --basetemp so query CLI tests do not match
  &quot;build&quot; inside the OBS user name abuild
- Requires(post/postun): update-alternatives for the
  graphify / graphify-mcp alternatives scriptlets</comment>
    <requestid>1372894</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>61feeada65ad00c238b4da9fbdaba139</srcmd5>
    <version>0.9.49</version>
    <time>1787656798</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Supersedes sr#1373460 (0.9.49). Same version bump, plus two changes on top.

Switch from update-alternatives to libalternatives (alts), the Factory
default: graphify and graphify-mcp are now declared in
%{_datadir}/libalternatives/&lt;name&gt;/1313.conf and %{_bindir}/&lt;name&gt; is a real
symlink to alts, so nothing runs at install time. The only scriptlet left is
%pre, which drops a stale update-alternatives entry on upgrade. The two
generic names are grouped separately on purpose - graphify-mcp lives in an
optional subpackage, so a shared group would name a member that need not be
installed.

Fix the primary-flavour Provides, which never worked: the spec used
%python3_only, which expands to a test for a flavour literally named
&quot;python3&quot;. No real flavour is called that (python313, python314), so the body
was silently dropped and the built RPM never provided the plain &quot;graphifyy&quot;
name. Replaced with a %{python_flavor} == %{primary_python} test, and the same
Provides added for graphifyy-mcp on the mcp subpackage. Verified against the
built RPMs: python313-graphifyy provides &quot;graphifyy = 0.9.49&quot; exactly once,
python313-graphifyy-mcp provides &quot;graphifyy-mcp = 0.9.49&quot;, and neither name
appears on the python314 flavour.

Built green on aarch64: 3908 tests passed per flavour, rpmlint 0 errors and
0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1373480</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>0fda598d7b20de672f0b068dd6f25fc5</srcmd5>
    <version>0.9.50</version>
    <time>1787766943</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.9.50. Refiled through the devel project after sr#1373736 was
declined for originating from a branch rather than a devel project; the
devel link is now registered as well (sr#1373768).

Source stays the GitHub tag archive rather than the PyPI sdist: the
0.9.50 sdist still omits ARCHITECTURE.md (read by
tests/test_architecture_doc.py) and 136 test files including
tests/fixtures/ and conftest.py, so it cannot run %check.

Licence re-derived and unchanged at Apache-2.0 AND MIT: LICENSE,
LICENSE-MIT and NOTICE are byte-identical to 0.9.49, and NOTICE still
records that pre-relicensing MIT contributions remain available under
LICENSE-MIT.

No dependency change was owed. The only non-version pyproject.toml
change is the optional [postgres] extra gaining tree-sitter-sql; that
extra is not packaged, python-tree-sitter-sql is not in Factory, and the
tests needing it use pytest.importorskip (confirmed SKIPPED in the build
log). No CVEs in the 0.9.49..0.9.50 range.

Verified on native aarch64 against openSUSE:Factory:ARM/standard: build
green, %check 3947 passed / 229 skipped / 82 deselected on both python313
and python314, rpmlint 0 errors / 0 badness (the 52 warnings are
python-missing-require on the deliberately-Recommends tree-sitter
grammars, unchanged from the 0.9.49 baseline).</comment>
    <requestid>1373778</requestid>
  </revision>
